rsz: retire a move type for the phase once a window of attempts accepted nothing

Policy candidate from the repair-knobs campaign (ideas/repair-knobs-nihl.md),
carried while it is measured; retires SKIP_GATE_CLONING if it dominates.
Not upstreamed.

On the designs where repair grinds, 90-96% of all candidates are
rejected (jpeg grt: 31523 tried, 2403 accepted), and the rejected ones
are dominated by move types that never fit the design. A type that has
been tried N times in a phase without one acceptance is retired for the
rest of the phase and comes back at the next. N defaults to 200 and
RSZ_MOVE_BUDGET overrides it while fitting, then it is frozen.

Chesterton's Fence: cloning exists because it wins on some designs
(riscv32i grt is 22% slower and 5.4 ps worse without it) and loses on
others (ibex cts is 28% faster without it), and SKIP_GATE_CLONING exists
because a user could see which case a design was. The acceptance window
sees the same thing per phase. The knob is left in place and still
honoured.

